00:45:16,551 --> 00:45:22,551
I Am Legend is a 2007 American post-apocalyptic action horror film directed by Francis Lawrence from
a screenplay by Akiva Goldsman and Mark Protosevich and starring Will Smith as U.S.

14
00:48:45,517 --> 00:48:51,517
Army virologist Robert Neville.

15
00:52:14,482 --> 00:52:20,482
Loosely based on the 1954 novel of the same name by Richard Matheson, the film is set in New York City after a virus, which was originally created
to cure cancer, has wiped out most of mankind, leaving Neville as the last human in New York City, other than nocturnal mutants.

16
00:55:43,448 --> 00:55:49,448
Immune to the virus, Neville works to develop a cure while
defending himself against the hostile mutants.

17
00:59:12,413 --> 00:59:18,413
It is the third feature-film adaptation of Matheson's novel following
1964's The Last Man on Earth and 1971's The Omega Man.

18
01:02:41,379 --> 01:02:47,379
Warner Bros.

19
01:06:10,344 --> 01:06:16,344
began developing I Am Legend in 1994, and various actors and directors were attached to the
project, though production was delayed due to budgetary concerns related to the script.

20
01:09:39,310 --> 01:09:45,310
Production began in 2006 in New York City, filming mainly on location in the
city, including a $5 million scene at the Brooklyn Bridge.

21
01:13:08,275 --> 01:13:14,275
I Am Legend was released on December 14, 2007, in the United States and Canada.

22
01:16:37,241 --> 01:16:43,241
It opened to the largest-ever box office (not adjusted for
inflation) for a non-Christmas film released in the U.S.

23
01:20:06,206 --> 01:20:12,206
in December, and was the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2007, earning $256 million
domestically and $329 million internationally for a total of $585 million.

24
01:23:35,172 --> 01:23:41,172
The film received generally positive reviews, with Smith's performance being singled out for praise,
while criticism focused on its divergences from the novel, particularly the ending.

